        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: die Einwanderung",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "die Einwanderung — \"immigration\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Die Stadt ist durch Einwanderung schnell gewachsen. The city has grown quickly through immigration."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From einwandern — to immigrate, with sein. Der Einwanderer — the immigrant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Einwanderung is the noun of einwandern \"to immigrate\", built on wandern \"to wander\", inherited from Old High German wandarōn and Proto-Germanic wandrōną (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
