          "title": "You'll want to know: die Flucht",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "die Flucht — \"flight, escape\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Nach der Flucht lebte die Familie zwei Jahre in einem Lager. After their flight the family lived in a camp for two years."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Auf der Flucht — on the run. The verb is fliehen — to flee."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Flucht is inherited from Middle High German vluht, Old High German fluht and Proto-Germanic fluhtiz \"flight\" (EtymDB), the noun of the verb for fleeing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
